        "id": "47e6783f-fd43-40b3-a4a8-c7aa3e9ac861",
        "content": "Totally agree with this. I used to think longer prompts = better context = better output. But in practice, I found that **the first 200 tokens matter most** — if those are clear, the rest is often noise.\n\nOne technique I use: \"Write a prompt that you would want to receive.\" This forces me to cut the fluff and focus on what actually matters.\n\nAnother insight: **structure beats length**. A 50-token prompt with clear sections often outperforms a 500-token wall of text.",
